From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: licheerv-nano: mux UART1 on the header

UART1 reaches the header through the IIC0 pads (XGPIOA[28]/[29]), where
UART1_TX/RX is function 1. Until now the pads were left to S31slip
through /dev/mem, but the shared config disables CONFIG_DEVMEM, so the
mux never happened and the HaLow modem saw nothing.

Add the pinctrl state so the modem link depends only on the DT. The
portal needs no board-specific code: it selects /dev/ttyS1 and the baud
as on every other board.

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2002-licheerv-nano-b.dts
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/input/linux-event-codes.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/pinctrl/pinctrl-sg2002.h>
 #include "sg2002.dtsi"
 
 / {
@@ -184,6 +185,24 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* UART1 is on XGPIOA[28]/[29] (the IIC0 pads, function 1). The slug
+ * between the controller and the header is the only board-specific part;
+ * S31slip and the portal then just use /dev/ttyS1 at the modem baud.
+ */
+&pinctrl {
+	uart1_cfg: uart1-cfg {
+		uart1-pins {
+			pinmux = <PINMUX(PIN_IIC0_SCL, 1)>,
+				 <PINMUX(PIN_IIC0_SDA, 1)>;
+			bias-pull-up;
+			drive-strength-microamp = <10800>;
+			power-source = <3300>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 &uart1 {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&uart1_cfg>;
 	status = "okay";
 };

